<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Entitlements for RoEnSpeak.app. build/build_macos.sh passes this file to codesign together
      with the hardened runtime option, both for the default ad hoc signature and for a real
      Developer ID.

      Full rationale, including what is deliberately absent (app sandbox, allow jit, apple
      events) and how the hardened runtime interacts with the Accessibility grant: BUILD.md,
      section "Signing and notarization (macOS)".

      Two entitlements, both load bearing:

        com.apple.security.device.audio.input (spelled with a dash below)
            Microphone access under the hardened runtime, declared at signing time so the
            NSMicrophoneUsageDescription prompt from Info.plist is honoured.

        com.apple.security.cs.disable.library.validation (spelled with dashes below)
            Lets the process load the whisper.cpp and ggml dylibs, Qt plugins, onnxruntime and
            PortAudio, none of which carry this app's Team ID; in an ad hoc build none carry a
            Team ID at all. Without it the Metal engine fails to load.

      Three rules for editing this file, none of which plutil lint catches but all of which
      codesign does, because codesign parses it with AMFIUnserializeXML:
        1. no comment before the root element,
        2. no angle brackets inside a comment,
        3. no doubled hyphen inside a comment (which is why the two keys are spelled with dots
           in this comment and with hyphens in the actual keys).
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
